==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|heafoc}}, {{l|ang|heafuc}} (''Mercian''), {{l|ang|hafuc}}

===Etymology===
From {{w|Anglo-Frisian}} ''*hæbuk'' [ˈhæ.βuk], from {{w|West Germanic}} ''*habuk'' [ˈhɑ.βuk], from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*habukaz}} [ˈxɑ.βu.kɑz]. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|havek}} ({{cog|fy|hauk}}), {{cog|osx|havuk}} ({{cog|nds|Haavk}}), {{cog|odt|havek}} ({{cog|nl|havik}}), {{cog|goh|habuh}} ({{cog|de|Habicht}}), {{cog|non|haukr}} ({{cog|sv|hök}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhɑ.fuk/|[ˈhɑ.vuk]|lang=ang}}

